ASC BRASS TABLET 5 CM. BGL., LANDSCAPED.0.7&#39; EAST OF BACK OF WALK ON EAST SIDE OF 109 STREET</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="684565219">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP278 Edmonton - 109 St.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ok, I meant to head home after Emily Murphy park but realized I would have to pass by a few more caps along the way.  I became a broken record this weekend with GJ....texting her I was on my way but I'm stopping for just one more.  lol  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I made it here and got distracted a bit before remembering the context pictures I had looked at for this one.  This became my first cap find I had to dig for.  My foot moved some dirt and I got a slight gleam of the cap.  Getting down I dug the rest of the mud cover off and was thrilled when I managed to decipher a few numbers.  I managed an ok pic of the cap, reapplied the mud cover and was on my way.....yes, with time for one more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683869763">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-05T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP278 Edmonton - 109 St.

Out for a lunch run to grab a few BCPs. Thought this one would be easy to spot since it was found a couple weeks ago. Not so much. A couple inches of dirt had migrated back over the cap. After some probing it was found and then after cleaning the numbers were good to read. I was surprised at how few muggles walked by me. 109 St was pretty solid with cars though. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="676904234">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="691070">UBC Geograd</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP278 Edmonton - 109 St.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice day for a lunch hour walk, so I headed up to this one. Reading previous logs, it appears that WillowZilla and company had done all the hard work finding this one, so I figured I'd ride their coattails and make the find. This proved to be a simple enough find thanks to their efforts- I first zeroed out on the utility cover, but after looking at the previously posted pictures I could determine exactly where it was.  Cap is in really rough shape- not much in the way of numbers to be deciphered, but it's certainly there.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680219689">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-09T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7338377">j0ckser</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP 278 Edmonton (109 Street)

Posted: N 53° 33.184 W 113° 30.493

My GPSr: N 53° 33.188 W 113° 30.496&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GeoGuider and I met up with Team WillowZilla today to do some brass caps. We brought along a bag full of tools. Tim brought along a long screw driver that he BVPete left behind at a brass cap somewhere along the way. For this cap, the metal detector found many wires underground and was pinging a lot. The long screwdriver found the brass cap, then we cleaned it up with some of our tools. The numbers on the cap are unreadable - its too bashed. Thanks for the cap outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="676396775">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-09T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1095439">GeoGuider</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP 278 Edmonton (109 Street)&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;Posted:  N 53° 33.184 W 113° 30.493&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;My GPSr:  N 53° 33.188 W 113° 30.496&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;j0ckser and I met up with WillowZilla and Tim today to do some brass caps.  We brought along a bag full of tools.  Tim brought along a long screw driver that he BVPete left behind at a brass cap somewhere along the way.  For this cap, the metal detector found many wires underground and was pinging a lot.  The long screwdriver found the brass cap, then we cleaned it up with some of our tools.  We thought we'd do this one early on a Sunday morning when there wouldn't be much traffic.  HA!  People get up way earlier than we did.  Thanks for the fun we've had over the years doing brass caps outforthehunt.  We REALLY appreciate all the work you've done to keep this site going.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
      <groundspeak:travelbugs />
